    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113998" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῑλίαρχ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>captain over a thousand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				304
			</span></i>: esp. <i>commandant</i> of a garrison, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.1.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Oec.</u>
				4.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χιλιάρχης</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.19.1
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Inscr.Magn.</u>
				157b
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A. D.)</span>, etc. (the usual form in this sense).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> title of Persian
			court official, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Art.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				1.21
			</span></i>; also in Macedonia, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				18.48
			</span></i>.</div>
